## Audience
The estimate is written for the audience `{{ audience }}`. This changes the framing, never the
estimation rules, the mandatory structure or the numbers.
{% if audience == "executive" %}
- Readers are executives or sponsors: lead with business outcomes, give ranges rather than false
  precision, and state the main risks and their mitigations in plain language.
- Keep technical jargon to a minimum and keep the breakdown short and high-level.
{% elif audience == "pm" %}
- Readers are project or delivery managers: organise the work in phases with milestones, name the
  dependencies between them, and make the team and duration easy to plan against.
- Mention who is involved in each phase and what is delivered.
{% elif audience == "developer" %}
- Readers are engineers: give a technical breakdown by component (services, data, integrations,
  infrastructure, tests) and state the technical assumptions explicitly.
- Name the riskiest technical assumption of each major area.
{% endif %}
